        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "chest_drainage_system_underwater_seal_drain_subsection_17",
          "subsection_title": "Common OSCE questions and model answers",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "chest_drainage_system_underwater_seal_drain_group_19",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q1. What is the principle of an underwater seal drain?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It provides a one-way pathway for air and fluid to leave the pleural space while preventing atmospheric air from returning through the water seal."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q2. Why must the drainage unit be below chest level?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "This reduces the risk of fluid flowing backwards towards the patient and supports gravity drainage."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q3. What is tidaling?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It is respiratory fluctuation of the water level in the water-seal chamber, reflecting pressure changes transmitted through the system. Its presence or absence must be interpreted in context."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q4. What does continuous bubbling mean?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It may indicate a persistent air leak from the patient or a leak in the drainage system. I would assess the patient, inspect the connections and escalate according to the clinical protocol."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q5. Why should a chest drain not be routinely clamped?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Clamping can prevent air from escaping and cause a tension pneumothorax when an ongoing air leak is present."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q6. What would you do if drainage suddenly stopped?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "I would assess the patient immediately, inspect the tubing for kinks or obstruction, review the water-seal behaviour and seek urgent assistance if obstruction or clinical deterioration is suspected. I would not strip the tubing or manipulate the system indiscriminately."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q7. What is the difference between a water-seal chamber and a suction-control chamber?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The water seal acts as a one-way valve. The suction-control chamber or mechanism regulates the prescribed negative pressure when suction is being used."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q8. What would you do if the patient suddenly became breathless?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "I would assess airway, breathing and circulation, provide urgent support according to the emergency protocol, check the drain and escalate immediately. I would consider tension pneumothorax among the possible causes."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "chest_drainage_system_underwater_seal_drain_subsection_18",
          "subsection_title": "Common mistakes and examiner tips",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "chest_drainage_system_underwater_seal_drain_group_20",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Common mistakes"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Placing the drainage unit above chest level."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Failing to inspect the tubing from patient to unit."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Confusing the water-seal chamber with the collection chamber."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Assuming all bubbling is abnormal."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Assuming absence of tidaling always means obstruction."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Routinely clamping, stripping or milking the tube."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Ignoring sudden fresh blood drainage."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Assessing the apparatus without assessing the patient."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Examiner tips"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Start by assessing the patient, not just the equipment."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Identify the collection chamber, water seal and suction-control mechanism."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Explain the significance and limitations of bubbling and tidaling."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "State that the unit should remain upright and below chest level."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Explicitly mention that routine clamping is unsafe."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Document drainage volume and character, respiratory observations and any escalation."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "chest_drainage_system_underwater_seal_drain_subsection_19",
          "subsection_title": "Mini-OSCE practice station",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "chest_drainage_system_underwater_seal_drain_group_21",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Practice station",
                    "Scenario"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A patient with a pneumothorax has a chest tube connected to an underwater seal drainage system. During your ward assessment, you notice continuous bubbling in the water-seal chamber."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Your tasks"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Identify the equipment and explain its principle."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Name its main components."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Explain two possible causes of continuous bubbling."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Describe your immediate assessment and next steps."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "State two important safety precautions."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
